{:event/body "2026-07-23、gftdcojp系プロダクトライン(cloud-itonami/cloud-murakumo/cloud-manimani/network-isekai/app-aozora)の運営法人としてAWAI Network, L.L.C.(Delaware LLC)を記録。entity type=Delaware LLC, 設立日=2026-07-20, Delaware州ファイル番号=10704996, EIN取得予定期間=08/12-09/24, registered agent=Legalinc Corporate Services Inc.(131 Continental Dr Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713 US、有効期限2027-07-20)。これは本ADRが記す『gftdcojp自身のGLEIF LEIベースformal identity record』とは別物(GLEIF LEI未取得のため引き続きblocked)であり、operating-entity(実際に事業を運営する法人)としての事実記録のみ。代表者個人情報(氏名/電話/住所)はオーナー指示によりADR/ledgerに記録しない。同じくAWAI Network, L.L.C.はjk-luxury org傘下のclub-shinshi/net-babinikuの運営主体としても記録(adr-2607062300-jk-luxury-org-club-shinshi-net-babiniku-relocation amend、JK Inc.(BVI)を置き換え)。", :adr/related ["adr-2607062300-jk-luxury-org-club-shinshi-net-babiniku-relocation"], :adr/id "adr-2607141600-cloud-itonami-real-entity-record-placement", :event/summary "cloud-itonami/cloud-murakumo/cloud-manimani/network-isekai/app-aozora operating entity recorded: AWAI Network, L.L.C.(Delaware LLC)", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-23T08:36:05.247Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :amend, :event/seq 32}
{:event/body "Files changed: wasm/aozora_create_session.kotoba, wasm/aozora_create_record.kotoba (resp-ptr alloc 512->2048 bytes, and the corresponding cap arguments passed to http-post/http-post-headers), both recompiled via kotoba.runtime/wasm-binary. Doc comments in these two files, test/wasm/aozora_create_session_test.clj, test/wasm/aozora_create_record_test.clj, and src/kawaraban/wasm_orchestrator.clj updated to record the new buffer size. No change to any offset math (resp-ptr is the LAST allocation in both modules). Implementation PR: etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kawaraban (see repo for PR number).", :adr/related ["adr-2607231711-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-phase-h-production-url-golive"], :adr/id "adr-2607231711-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-phase-h-production-url-golive", :event/summary "Go-live diagnostic (2026-07-23) against the real production PDS found a real bug this ADR's own recompile exposed: aozora_create_session.kotoba/aozora_create_record.kotoba's resp-ptr buffer (512 bytes) was too small for real AT-Proto responses -- kototama.tender's write-bytes! silently returns -1 on overflow, INDISTINGUISHABLE from a refused call. Empirically confirmed: the full CACAO self-mint -> wire-encode -> createSession chain was already working correctly end-to-end against the live pds.aozora.app (status 200, genuine session minted, real accessJwt/refreshJwt in a 694-byte response) -- the -1 was purely the response buffer being too small to read the (perfectly valid) reply, not an auth or wire-format failure. Fixed by widening both modules' resp-ptr from 512 to 2048 bytes (the last allocation in each module, so no other offsets shift). Verified against the real server post-fix: written=694, refused=false, real accessJwt extracted correctly via extract-access-jwt. 136 tests / 295 assertions still green.", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-23T08:46:42.699Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :amend, :event/seq 33}
{:event/body "Files changed (same PR as the buffer-size fix, or a follow-up PR -- see repo): src/kawaraban/wasm_orchestrator.clj (write-record-field! now takes+enforces max-bytes; new record-field-widths map; create-record-via-wasm! rewritten to use a uniform w! helper and return :truncated-fields instead of the old single :headline-truncated? key). test/kawaraban/wasm_orchestrator_test.clj (updated 2 existing tests for the new :truncated-fields shape, added test-create-record-via-wasm-truncates-an-overlong-article-url-instead-of-corrupting-memory as a direct regression test for the live-observed corruption). No wasm recompile needed for this fix (Clojure-side only).", :adr/related ["adr-2607231711-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-phase-h-production-url-golive"], :adr/id "adr-2607231711-kawaraban-kotoba-wasm-phase-h-production-url-golive", :event/summary "Second go-live diagnostic finding+fix (2026-07-23, same live-run session): a real 78-byte BBC article URL exceeded record.cites.0.url's 64-byte field width in aozora_create_record.kotoba, and was written RAW (no truncation) -- corrupting the next field's length header. Observed live: a genuinely published record (rkey art.outlet.bbc-world.1784766113) with control bytes embedded mid-URL. Root cause: unlike the analysis/headline field (already correctly truncate-utf8'd), cites0/cites1 were written via write-record-field! with no bound check at all. Fixed write-record-field! to require+enforce a max-bytes parameter (truncate-utf8) for every field, structurally closing this class of bug for all 9 fields, not just the 2 that happened to overflow this time. While fixing this, caught and fixed a SECOND, independent bug introduced by the first fix attempt: the function parameter named identity shadows clojure.core/identity, so the initial (keep identity [...]) construction for :truncated-fields silently treated each vector element as a key lookup into the identity map, always returning empty -- corrected to (remove nil? ...). Caught only because a new regression test asserted the specific field, not merely that the call didn't error. 137 tests / 299 assertions green (1 new test). No real network calls made while iterating on this fix.", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-23T09:08:21.221Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :amend, :event/seq 34}
{:event/body "cloud-itonami isic/isco/iso3166/unspsc/cofog/gtin wave (294 repos) の not-yet-actionable 判定は変わらず。native-AOT対応はrecord/variant値表現が皆無なため独立した大型後続イニシアチブと判明、次はその基礎作業に着手する方針", :adr/related ["2607231830"], :adr/id "2607202200", :event/summary "kotoba-lang/compiler ADR 0050-0061 (全merge済み) が state capability kit のCanonical ABI境界越えと初の実providerロジックを実Wasmtime実行で証明。gap-disposition (a) の文字列primitiveギャップは解消。(b) の :wasm-aot :pending は意図的に維持 (native-AOT/JIT完全未着手・他6kit未実装のため)。詳細は90-docs/adr/2607231830参照", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-23T09:32:23.662Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 35}
{:event/seq 36, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-24T04:22:57.443Z", :adr/id "adr-2607242100-cloud-itonami-awai-network-operator-change", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Sharpened the operator-change gaps with cited research (child commit 7f56df7b): foreign-company registration under Companies Act Art. 818 is likely required for an ongoing Japan-targeted subscription business (not merely open) and is now the highest-priority item, with a PE tax-exposure caveat; consumption tax likely does NOT require JCT registration given cloud-itonami is B2B-only (Japan's reverse-charge mechanism applies instead), and a customer reverse-charge notice was added to legal/terms.md Section 6.3; the prior pass's APPI citation was wrong (Article 24, cross-border transfer OUT of Japan) and is corrected to Article 171 (extraterritorial application), a narrower/simpler finding. Also added legal/payment-collection-agency-agreement.md, an unsigned DRAFT documenting Gftd Japan's Stripe account collecting on AWAI Network's behalf -- makes the Stripe merchant-of-record mismatch a concrete, reviewable document without claiming it resolves anything until executed. None of this is legal advice; every item still needs counsel review. manifest/west.yml pin advanced --entry cloud-itonami (7f56df7becd6, server-side verified).", :adr/related ["2607232200"]}
{:event/body "orgs/kotoba-lang/bim の west pin が 2275f22f(212コミット遅れ)で止まっており、GitHub main(7f4f4b8)には未記録の進捗が既に着地していた。pinをfast-forwardで7f4f4b8へ前進(manifest/west.yml、commit 8f58339、単独diff)。判明した実際の状態:\\n\\n item 2(plate/shell bending): 完了。PR #128 が ロッキングフリーのDKT(Discrete Kirchhoff Triangle)plate-bending要素を追加(analyze-plate-bending-mesh)。片持ち梁閉形式収束・単純支持正方形板のTimoshenko&Woinowsky-Krieger係数との比較(0.18%以内)・全体力の釣り合い・Maxwell-Betti相反定理(13桁一致)の4通りで独立検証済み。design-code半分は既にPR #127で完了(structural-member-utilization)。残存gap: 3D flat shell要素(membrane+bending結合、3D埋め込み)は未着手 -- 現状はローカル2D平面のplate定式化のみ。\\n\\n item 3(exact hidden-line + production documentation): 部分完了。PR #129が実多角形重なり判定によるhidden-line occlusionを追加(旧来のAABB厳密部分集合判定を置換、Sutherland-Hodgman clipping)。残存gap: 複数遮蔽物の合成判定は未対応(1つのより近い多角形が単独でカバーする場合のみ判定)、レンダリングは依然bounding-boxで実シルエット輪郭ではない、PDF export(bim.interchange)はocclusion culling自体が無い、dimensions/tags/schedules/sheet構成は未着手。\\n\\n item 5(external IFC corpus拡張 + formal buildingSMART certification process): 未着手を確認。main tip までの219コミット全件のコミットメッセージを検索したが該当作業なし。\\n\\n item 6(Revit-origin acceptance scenario): 完了 + follow-up。PR #130が実在するAutodesk Revit Architecture 2011のIFC2X3 export(test/fixtures/external/revit2011_wall1.ifc、org-iso-16739外部コーパスと共有)を使い、import→property編集→export→再importでのsemantics/geometry比較を実施し2つの実バグを発見(1つは同PRで修正、1つはドキュメント化のみ)。PR #131がCSG half-space meshのクラッシュ2件(2D profile-position/chained half-space clip)を修正。PR #132がIfcRelVoidsElementのopening情報がimport importedElementに伝播しない欠落を修正。残存gap: 角度付き(mitered)cut形状に対するCSG mesh clippingの根本バグは未修正のまま明示的にドキュメント化されている(perpendicular以外の半空間クリップは現状の区間短縮ショートカットでは表現できない、より大きい別課題として温存)。\\n\\nこのADRの実質的な残存gapは: item 2の3D flat shell embedding、item 3の複数遮蔽物合成判定/真のシルエット描画/PDF occlusion/production annotation一式、item 5全体、item 6のangled-cut CSG mesh clippingバグ、の4点に絞られる。", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"], :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/summary "Gap-order items 2/3/6 already substantially done upstream (unrecorded); item 5 confirmed still open; west pin was 212 commits stale", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-24T04:52:37.886Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 37}
{:event/seq 38, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-24T08:00:48.092Z", :adr/id "2607211343", :event/actor "agent (Claude Code session, owner Jun Kawasaki)", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "1M-datom merkle-lsm gate run: first sub-linear peak-RSS evidence past 100k (6.93GB at 1M vs ~4.88GB at 100k); 10M gate still open", :event/body "2026-07-24, merkle-lsm-bench (clojure -J-Xmx16g -M:merkle-bench 1000000, writers=32, Apple M4 32GB / OpenJDK 21): 1,000,000 datoms build+compact, zero row loss, total 907.5s (compaction 745s), throughput 1,102 rows/s, peak RSS 6,927,368,192 bytes. 10x the 100k data volume cost 1.42x the RSS -- first measured (not extrapolated) support for the P1 sub-linear-RSS gate direction. Full receipt: kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer bench/results/2026-07-24-merkle-lsm-1m.edn (merged ba9e860). A same-day 10M attempt (-Xmx20g) was externally terminated on the shared workstation before producing output -- per this ADR's own rule the 10M gate remains open and must be measured, not extrapolated. Related same-day serving-layer work: net-kotobase kotobase-cf-wasm read caching (block cache + chain-cid-keyed read-response cache) cut live repeat-read CPU from ~1550ms to 24ms; the remaining cache-miss hydration floor is exactly the hydrate-db-cached / cold-datoms-async wiring gap this ADR tracks."}
{:event/seq 39, :event/type :correction, :event/at "2026-07-24T08:02:01.986Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211343-kotobase-merkle-lsm-production-gap-closure", :event/actor "agent (Claude Code session, owner Jun Kawasaki)", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "corrects event seq 38's :adr/id join key (this ADR's :adr/id is the long form; the short '2607211343' cannot join to the base file). Content of seq 38 stands: 1M merkle-lsm gate run, sub-linear RSS evidence, 10M gate open", :event/body "See :event/seq 38 (same day) for the full note: 1M-datom merkle-lsm-bench run measured peak RSS 6.93GB at 1M vs ~4.88GB at 100k (10x data -> 1.42x RSS, first measured sub-linear evidence); receipt in kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer bench/results/2026-07-24-merkle-lsm-1m.edn (ba9e860); 10M attempt externally terminated, gate remains open and must be measured."}
{:event/seq 40, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-24T13:07:29.161Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211343-kotobase-merkle-lsm-production-gap-closure", :event/actor "owner decision via agent (Claude Code session)", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "P1 10M gate re-scoped by owner decision (2026-07-24): no monolithic in-memory 10M run; measured 2-point slope is the evidence, gate applies to the future streaming/spill compaction", :event/body "Owner decision during live session: the 10M single-JVM in-memory compaction run was stopped (twice-launched, killed) as low-information -- the measured slope from the two existing receipts (100k: 4.88GB peak RSS; 1M: 6.93GB, kotobase-peer bench/results/2026-07-24-merkle-lsm-1m.edn) is ~2.3KB/datom above a ~4.5GB JVM+harness floor, so 10M in-memory needs roughly +23GB over the floor and cannot fit a reasonable heap; running it to OOM adds no design information, and smaller runs (2M, or 2k) add none either (2k sits entirely below the fixed-overhead floor). Production serving never compacts 10M in one process anyway (materialized-view/R2 path is the serving-scale route, benchmarked separately). Consequence for P1: the sub-linear-RSS gate is NOT closed -- it is re-scoped to the future streaming/spill (O(partition) peak RSS) compaction design, which must be measured when it exists; claiming 10M readiness on the current pure in-memory compact-runs-partitioned remains prohibited, now backed by measurement rather than absence of measurement."}
{:event/body "ADR-2607198300 は『この native backend は kgraph-assert!/kgraph-query（EAVT datom-store capability）をまだサポートしない』と記載していたが、2026-07-24 の kotoba-lang/compiler 実地調査で backend/x86_64.cljc（797行）と backend/aarch64.cljc（735行）が kgraph op 群を実装済みであり、test/kotoba/compiler/native_executor_test.clj の kgraph-native-customer-pilot-asserts-and-queries-through-real-kexe-loader が実ネイティブ実行で assert/get/count/entity-at を検証していることを確認した。この capability gap を理由にした native 経路の回避は不要。関連する正準トポロジーと設計クリーンアップは ADR-2607241100 を参照。", :adr/related ["adr-2607241100-kotoba-stack-topology-and-design-cleanup"], :adr/id "adr-2607198300-kotoba-native-aot-execution-tier-discovery-and-no-bypass-policy", :event/summary "native backend kgraph gap は解消済み — x86_64/aarch64 backend が kgraph-assert!/kgraph-get/kgraph-count/kgraph-entity-at を実装、native_executor_test の kgraph-native-customer-pilot が実 kexe loader 実行で証明（2026-07-24 実測、compiler docs/adr/0074 起票時確認）", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-24T13:11:20.114Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :amend, :event/seq 41}
{:event/seq 42, :event/type :amend, :event/at "2026-07-24T14:34:49.207Z", :adr/id "adr-2607246000-adult-content-payment-processor-banking-jurisdiction-research", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "PIライセンス設立費用のJPY換算を追加、EMIとの対比を明確化(2026-07-24レート)", :event/body "## Addendum: JPY換算 + PI(EMIではなくPayment Institution)であることの明確化（2026-07-24）\n\n前回記録した Round 6 の設立費用比較表は既に **PI(Payment Institution)** のデータであり EMI ではない（EMIは表内「同国EMI費用との比較」行として対比目的でのみ別掲していた）。本追記は (a) その区別を再確認し、(b) 全数値を日本円換算して併記する。\n\n使用レート（2026-07-24 時点の概算、WebSearch取得。日々変動するため実務では発注時点のレートで再計算すること）: EUR/JPY ≈ 186、USD/JPY ≈ 163.8、GEL/JPY ≈ 62.5（GEL/USD ≈ 0.381 経由の算出）。\n\n### PIライセンス設立費用（JPY換算、EUR/USD/GEL原数値と併記）\n\n| 項目 | リトアニア(PI) | マルタ(PI) | ジョージア(PSP) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PI資本要件(法定) | €20,000/50,000/125,000 → 約372万円/930万円/2,325万円 | 同左（PSD2同一体系）→ 約372万円/930万円/2,325万円 | 未確認(要現地弁護士確認) |\n| 規制当局申請料(法定) | €1,463(フルPI)/€693(AISPのみ) → 約27.2万円/約12.9万円 | €3,500 → 約65.1万円 | 5,000〜10,000 GEL → 約31.3万円〜62.5万円 |\n| 年間監督料(法定) | 情報源に明記なし | 総資産×0.0002、最低€2,500/年 → 最低約46.5万円/年 | 情報源に明記なし |\n| 法人設立費用 | 約€1,200 → 約22.3万円(最低資本金€1,000は別途) | €1,000〜3,000(初年度合計約€3,200) → 約18.6万円〜55.8万円(初年度合計約59.5万円) | 現実的予算2,500〜3,000 GEL → 約15.6万円〜18.8万円、即時利用可の既製会社€1,180 → 約22.0万円 |\n| コンサル/法務費(業者見積り) | €20,000〜25,000(Crassula社見積り中心) → 約372万円〜465万円 | €50,000〜150,000(Gonzi & Associates社見積り中心) → 約930万円〜2,790万円 | 具体的見積り情報源なし、弁護士時給$150〜500(約2.5万円〜8.2万円/時)の一般相場のみ |\n| 現地拠点・人員コスト | 現地居住取締役・MLRO・リスク/ITリード必須、金額個別記載なし | 現地から実質指揮する最低2名要件あり、金額情報源になし | 情報源に記載なし |\n| 総額(初年度・現実的見積り) | €200,000〜350,000 → 約3,720万円〜6,510万円 | 規制費用€26,000〜131,000(資本除く) + 法務費€50,000〜150,000 ≒ 概算€100,000〜280,000 → 約1,860万円〜5,208万円(資本要件分は別途最大€125,000≒2,325万円上乗せ) | ソフトウェア開発/購入だけで$25,000〜100,000 → 約410万円〜1,638万円。トータル見積りは算出不可 |\n| 取得期間 | 法定3ヶ月、実務6〜12ヶ月 | 完全書類提出後3〜6ヶ月 | 60日(不備時+30日、複雑案件+30日、最大120日) |\n\n### 参考: 同国EMI(Electronic Money Institution)の費用（PIとの対比・JPY換算）\n\n| 項目 | リトアニア(EMI) | マルタ(EMI) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 資本要件(法定) | €350,000 → 約6,510万円 | €350,000 → 約6,510万円 |\n| 規制当局申請料(法定) | €1,463 → 約27.2万円(PIフルと同額) | €10,000 → 約1,860万円(PIの€3,500=約65.1万円より高い) |\n| コンサル/法務費 | €20,000〜25,000 → 約372万円〜465万円(PIとほぼ同水準) | 情報源に個別記載なし |\n| 総額(初年度) | €250,000〜400,000 → 約4,650万円〜7,440万円(PIより資本要件・総コストとも重い) | 資本のみでPIの2.8倍(€350k vs 125k上限)、申請料もPIの約2.9倍 |\n\n### 結論（要点）\n\n- PIはEMIに比べ、**資本要件が最大でも1/2.8(€125,000 vs €350,000)、リトアニアの申請料はほぼ同額だがマルタの申請料はPIの方が約1/2.9安い**——「acquiring/カード発行までやりたいがEMI水準の巨額資本は避けたい」場合、PSD2フル階層のPI(€125,000)が現実的な下限ライン。\n- 円換算した場合、リトアニアPIの初年度現実的総額は**約3,720万円〜6,510万円**、マルタPIは**約1,860万円〜5,208万円(資本要件次第でさらに最大2,325万円上乗せ)**、ジョージアPSPは規制費用自体は**数十万円〜百万円台と最も安いが、法務費・現地拠点コストの情報源が最も薄く総額算出不可**——「安く見える」が実際には現地弁護士への個別見積りなしに総額を確定できない点は前回同様の注意点として維持する。\n- 為替レートは常時変動するため、実際の予算組みでは発注直前に最新レートで再計算すること。本追記のJPY数値はあくまで2026-07-24時点の概算レンジ感を示すもの。"}
{:event/body "kotoba-lang/stripe-ops repo built (governor/phase/operation/store/stripeport/advisor/sim, 21 tests / 82 assertions, clj-kondo 0 errors/warnings), pushed to GitHub, registered in west (manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects + west.yml --entry, pin verified reachable from main). Integration into orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami landed as PR #481 (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami, merge commit fa3de1dd): 3 new ReAct-agent tools (itonami_stripe_lookup / itonami_stripe_create_payment_link / itonami_stripe_confirm_payment_link) in cloud_itonami.agent, wired via cli.cljs's build-stripe-ops-actor (mock-stripeport default; live-stripeport opt-in only when STRIPE_OPS_RESTRICTED_KEY is present in env). Verified end-to-end: direct smoke test of the lookup/propose/confirm flow against mock-stripeport, backward-compat confirmed (omitting :stripe-ops-actor yields the original 3-tool list unchanged), clj-kondo clean on both edited cloud-itonami files, shadow-cljs agent-cli build compiles and the resulting CLI starts cleanly. cloud-itonami's own :test runner is currently broken for unrelated, pre-existing reasons (confirmed via git stash that the identical compile error -- engine-db/fresh-conn missing var in cloud_itonami/ops.cljc -- exists on main without this change). Outstanding: the Stripe Dashboard restricted-API-key creation itself (Customers/Subscriptions/Products/Prices read + Payment Links write only) was deliberately NOT performed by the agent (credential-form safety floor) -- this remains the owner's manual step before live-stripeport can be used; the actor runs mock-only until then.", :adr/related ["2607161745"], :adr/id "2607242700", :event/summary "Implementation completed: kotoba-lang/stripe-ops built+pushed, wired into cloud-itonami as ReAct agent tools, restricted API key creation left as owner's manual step", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-24T14:37:05.998Z", :event/actor "Claude (agent session)", :event/type :note, :event/seq 43}
{:event/body "## Addendum: 具体的な法律・手続き + cloud-itonami実装状況の確認（2026-07-25）\n\n### 1. PIライセンスの根拠法・手続き（一次資料ベース、確度を明記）\n\n**リトアニア(PI) — 確度:高(一次資料あり)**\n- 根拠法: Republic of Lithuania Law on Payment Institutions No. XI-549（リトアニア決済機関法）+ Law on Payments。PSD2(Directive (EU) 2015/2366)国内法化、2018-08-01施行。出典: https://e-seimas.lrs.lt/portal/legalAct/lt/TAD/0b531920890111eb998483d0ae31615c 、EUR-Lex国内法化記録: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=NIM:258682\n- 規制当局: Lietuvos bankas(リトアニア中銀)。https://www.lb.lt/en/authorisation-of-payment-institutions\n- 手続き: ①リトアニア法人設立 → ②中銀へ申請 → ③5営業日の形式審査(受理可否) → ④実体審査(取締役/主要株主fit-and-proper・事業計画・AML/CFTプログラム・資金保全体制・資本証明) → ⑤海外発行書類はApostille必須 → ⑥認可決定\n- 法定審査期間: 完全な申請から3ヶ月(PSD2 Art.12)。実務6〜12ヶ月。\n\n**マルタ(PI) — 確度:中(規制当局PDFは403で直接未確認、法律事務所解説で裏付け)**\n- 根拠法: Financial Institutions Act, Chapter 376 (Laws of Malta)。PSD2＋EMD2(Directive 2009/110/EC)国内法化、MFSA発行Financial Institutions Rulesが細則。出典(二次): https://www.mondaq.com/financial-services/837992/psd2-implemented-into-maltese-law-what-now 、https://gvzh.mt/insights/psd2-implemented-maltese-law/\n- 規制当局: MFSA(Malta Financial Services Authority)\n- 手続き: ①MFSA事前面談(任意) → ②マルタ法人設立 → ③正式申請(事業計画・ガバナンス体制・リスク管理/AML方針・取締役等Personal Questionnaire・3年財務予測+ストレステスト・自己資本計算・ITセキュリティ質問票) → ④MFSAレビュー(反復照会あり) → ⑤条件付き仮認可 → ⑥条件充足後に本認可\n- 期間: 完全提出後3〜6ヶ月。「6ヶ月超過で自動却下」規則は前回記録の通りだが本ラウンドでは一次資料未再確認。\n\n**ジョージア(PSP) — 確度:高(一次資料あり)、重大な構造的差異を確認**\n- 根拠法: Law of Georgia on Payment Systems and Payment Services(文書番号6304-Iს、2012-05-25採択・2012-07-01施行、以降改正)。出典(一次): https://matsne.gov.ge/en/document/view/1673253\n- 規制当局: National Bank of Georgia(NBG)。https://nbg.gov.ge/en/page/payment-service-providers-2\n- 登録義務者(Article 15/14(1)): PSPはNBGへの登録、または商業銀行/マイクロファイナンス機関として自動的に権限を持つ、のいずれか。\n- 手続き: ①ジョージア法人(LLC/JSC)設立+現地事務所登録 → ②NBGへ登録申請(登録料GEL 5,000証明・決済フロー図・電子システム/バックアップ詳細等) → ③NBG審査60日(不備時+30日、複雑案件+さらに30日、最大120日) → ④登録決議\n- 資本要件GEL 250,000の記述は二次資料のみで一次資料未確認(要個別確認)。\n\n### 2. パスポーティングの有無 — 最重要の構造的差異\n\n- **EU/EEA(リトアニア・マルタ)**: PSD2 Title II/Article 25に基づき、どちらか1国で取得したPIライセンスはEEA全域にパスポーティング可能(本国当局へ通知→ホスト国当局へ転送、再ライセンス不要)。出典: EBA https://www.eba.europa.eu/eba-response/6974 、CSSF https://www.cssf.lu/en/Document/opinion-of-the-european-banking-authority-on-the-nature-of-passport-notifications-regarding-agents-and-distributors-under-directive-eu-2015-2366-psd2-directive-2009-110-ec-emd2-and-directive-e/\n- **ジョージア**: パスポーティングは一切存在しない。法の適用範囲はジョージア国内のみで、EU/EEAとの相互承認メカニズムがない構造的制約。**ADR本文Round 5「ジョージア=非EUで最も信頼できる速い/安いワイルドカード」の位置づけは、この観点で訂正・限定が必要**——ジョージアPSP登録はジョージア国内決済業務の許可であって、EU PIが持つEEA全域acquiring権の代替にはならない。\n\n### 3. cloud-itonamiの実装状況（自社PSP運営の座組との照合）\n\n| 項目 | 状態 | 根拠(repo/ADR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 設立手続きコンサル | 実装済み、ただし会社登記のみでライセンス取得支援は含まない | `cloud-itonami-isic-6910`「Global Incorporation Actor」(Registrar-LLM ⊣ RegistrarGovernor)、`src/formation/`(advisor/governor/phase/registry/store)、25テスト/111アサーション。R0範囲は10法域(JPN/USA-DE/GBR/DEU/EST/KOR/IND/SGP/NZL/CAN)のみ、政府ポータル/KYCプロバイダ/決済連携は未接続。west.yml未登録のstandalone repo |\n| 銀行業務(預金・AML/KYC・決済・SWIFT等) | 実装済み(maturity :implemented) | `cloud-itonami-isic-6419`、`src/banking/` |\n| 与信/融資 | 実装済み | `cloud-itonami-isic-6492`、`src/credit/`、人間承認ゲート付き引受/実行アクター |\n| カード決済処理・清算(acquiring最寄り) | 実装済み | `cloud-itonami-isic-6619`、`src/card/`、intake・不正審査・清算・チャージバック保留解除 |\n| EMI/PI(電子マネー発行・ウォレットcustody) | 存在しない | ISIC 6499の枠は無関係なVCファンド・アクターに転用済み。専用repo/ADR/コードなし |\n\n注意: 上記4リポ(`isic-6419`/`-6492`/`-6619`/`-6910`)は本superprojectのworking treeには未取得(`west update`未実行)、GitHub上に存在するのみ確認済み。ローカル`orgs/`配下にあるのは`cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger`のみ(資金移動・口座保持をせず実際の実行は`isic-6492`/`isic-6419`に委譲する設計)。\n\n結論: cloud-itonamiには銀行業務・与信・カード決済処理の実装済みアクターが既に存在するが、EMI/PI(電子マネー発行体)そのものと、金融ライセンス取得支援コンサルは未実装。本ADR(2607246000)は純粋な市場調査であり、対応する製品コードは存在しない。net-babiniku等の決済戦略検討でcloud-itonamiの既存アクター(isic-6419/6492/6619)を土台に使う場合は、それらが未登録のstandalone repoでありwest.yml登録・ローカルcheckoutから着手が必要な点に留意する。", :adr/related ["2607031500"], :adr/id "adr-2607246000-adult-content-payment-processor-banking-jurisdiction-research", :event/summary "PIライセンスの根拠法・手続き・パスポーティング差異を追記、cloud-itonamiのEMI/PI/銀行/コンサル実装状況を確認", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-24T14:42:40.962Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :amend, :event/seq 44}
{:event/seq 45, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-23T10:02:58.142Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Gap-order item 5, achievable half: kotoba-lang/org-iso-16739 PR #51 (merged 152df8a). Re-verified all 3 existing external test tiers fresh: pinned corpus (21 files/139 products, lossless, matches ADR's stated evidence), external IfcOpenShell schema/WHERE-rule validator (0 errors), and -- new -- the FULL LIVE buildingSMART IDS 1.0 implementer corpus cloned fresh from upstream (not just the pinned local subset), which has grown to 291 cases (from 287 previously assumed) and surfaced 3 real conformance bugs: (1)+(2) property-requirement-matches? returned true unconditionally for existence-only checks, so an empty IFCLABEL or IFCLOGICAL(.U.) incorrectly satisfied 'property must be set' -- fixed by reusing the existing valid-attribute-value? predicate; (3) multiple <xs:pattern> facets in one <xs:restriction> should OR-combine per XSD but the parser overwrote :pattern per element so only the last ever applied -- fixed via an accumulating :patterns collection in parser+matcher+writer. All 3 fixes have network-free regression tests. Also added corpus-runner.clj's first-ever performance budget (previously zero performance testing existed in this repo) -- generous 30s ceiling on the full corpus round-trip, observed baseline ~19s. Post-fix: 291/291 IDS cases pass. Formal buildingSMART certification itself (the ADR's other ask in item 5) is NOT attempted -- it is an external submission/audit process requiring an actual organizational entity, not something achievable through code. Remaining: item 6 (Revit-origin acceptance scenario), which can now legitimately use the corpus's real Revit-exported IFC2X3 fixtures (Revit 2011/2014 wall/half-space exports) as its origin model.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
{:event/seq 46, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-23T10:21:18.765Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Gap-order item 6, final remaining item: kotoba-lang/bim PR #130 (merged 3350d7a). Real end-to-end acceptance scenario using an unmodified Autodesk Revit Architecture 2011 IFC2X3 wall export (same pinned file already used by org-iso-16739's corpus) -- import, edit a property, coordinate structural + drawings, export, reopen with an independent parse, compare semantics/geometry. Running it surfaced and fixed 2 real crashes: structural-shell-from-element and element-mesh both unconditionally assumed every :kind :wall element has the simple :geometry :axis/:profile shape bim/wall authors, throwing NPEs for imported foreign BREP geometry -- both now gracefully skip/fall-back instead (element-mesh falls back to the already-existing generic geometry-mesh dispatch that already handles :boolean-result, matching the pattern :slab already used). A 3rd, deeper bug was found and explicitly NOT fixed: meshing this wall's specific nested boolean-clipped half-space-solid (its mitered end) throws inside positioned-profile-boundary/boolean-result-mesh -- structural/drawing coordination is instead demonstrated on a companion analytical wall built from the imported wall's own Revit pset dimensions, with the gap documented directly in the test. A 4th, smaller gap also found+documented but not fixed: import-external-ifc drops IfcRelVoidsElement openings entirely. What the scenario DOES verify end-to-end and passing: edited property survives export+reopen, original :geometry survives byte-for-byte, companion wall structural shell + drawing render correctly. 145 tests/958 assertions, 0 lint errors. With this PR, ALL SIX gap-order items from this ADR have real, tested, merged work from this session: items 1 and 4 fully complete; items 2, 3, and 5 substantially complete with explicitly documented remaining sub-scope (plate/shell FEA done but membrane+3D-shell-embedding not; occlusion-decision fixed but rendering still bbox and PDF export uncovered; IDS corpus bugs fixed but formal buildingSMART certification is an external process outside agent scope); item 6 complete with 2 further gaps surfaced and documented rather than silently left unaddressed. Session total across bim/kami-app-bim-editor/org-iso-16739: PRs #63,64,65,125,126,127,128,129,130 (bim/editor) + #51 (org-iso-16739), all merged.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
{:event/seq 47, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-23T11:25:14.346Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Follow-up to item 6: kotoba-lang/bim PR #131 (merged 5cdc81c) precisely root-causes and partially fixes the CSG mesh crash PR #130 documented but left unfixed. Two real bugs fixed: (1) positioned-profile-boundary destructured a profile's own (frequently 2D, IfcAxis2Placement2D) :position :location into [px py pz] unconditionally, leaving pz nil for 2-element locations -- this was actually the FIRST NPE in the original crash chain, hit during boolean-result-mesh's eager speculative meshing of the unclipped extrusion, fixed by reusing the existing point3 2D/3D-padding helper; (2) clipped-extrusion's fallback only recognized a direct :extruded-area-solid first-operand, never resolving chains of more than one half-space clip (the standard IfcBooleanClippingResult pattern for e.g. a wall end cut by 2 planes) -- added resolve-clipped-extrusion to recurse through arbitrary chain depth. Both independently regression-tested with synthetic geometry. Re-verified against the Revit fixture: element-mesh no longer crashes. Precisely diagnosed remaining gap (NOT fixed): this wall's specific cut is genuinely angled/mitered (~5.7deg off perpendicular to the extrusion axis), and clipped-extrusion's strict near-1.0 dot-product check correctly rejects it since a non-perpendicular half-space cut needs a differently-shaped result (slanted end face) the current interval-shortening shortcut cannot produce -- true fix requires either general angled-plane mesh clipping or building a bounded proxy mesh from a polygonally-bounded half-space's own boundary polygon routed through the existing mesh-csg/mesh-boolean machinery. 147 tests/963 assertions, 0 lint errors. This is a real, incremental improvement over #130's finding, not a full resolution -- the angled-cut gap and the still-unfixed import-external-ifc opening-drop gap from #130 remain open, precisely documented follow-ups.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
{:event/seq 48, :event/type :note, :event/at "2026-07-24T00:38:42.134Z", :adr/id "adr-2607211437-kotoba-bim-revit-equivalent-architecture-session-close", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/summary "Second follow-up to item 6: kotoba-lang/bim PR #132 (merged 7f4f4b8) fixes the dropped-openings-on-import gap PR #130 documented but did not fix. Root cause: imported-element only calls attach-imported-openings (axis-relative offset/sill placement via bim/add-opening-to-wall) inside the branch for walls with simple directly-readable geometry -- a complex-geometry wall (e.g. Revit BREP) falls into the generic bim/element fallback that never called it, silently discarding any related openings, even though ifc.core's own parser (verified directly) already correctly resolves IfcRelVoidsElement onto the raw product. Fixed by always attaching raw opening products as a new, deliberately separate :ifc/openings field (not reusing :openings' rectangular-opening offset/sill/width/height shape, which wall-with-openings-mesh/add-opening-to-wall/remove-opening-from-wall depend on -- feeding those an incompatible shape risks silent wrong-answer overlap checks rather than a clean failure). 147 tests/965 assertions, 0 lint errors; acceptance scenario test extended to assert the opening now round-trips with its correct global-id. Remaining open, documented gaps from this session: angled/mitered half-space clipping (partially diagnosed in bim#131, not fixed -- needs general angled-plane mesh clipping or a bounded half-space proxy mesh through mesh-csg), true silhouette rendering vs bounding-box rectangles for drawings, PDF-export occlusion, 3D-shell embedding + membrane coupling for the plate-bending element. Formal buildingSMART certification remains outside agent scope.", :adr/related ["adr-2607122300-kami-engine-cad-org-iso-10303-positioning"]}
